WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.132
The laws of inheritance were

2
00:00:02.132 --> 00:00:04.295
found in a monastery garden.

3
00:00:04.295 --> 00:00:05.874
With pea plants.

4
00:00:06.208 --> 00:00:09.393
Gregor Mendel published his pea

5
00:00:09.393 --> 00:00:11.718
experiments in 1866.

6
00:00:11.718 --> 00:00:12.486
In 1908,

7
00:00:12.486 --> 00:00:15.389
Hardy and Weinberg described populations

8
00:00:15.389 --> 00:00:17.312
in genetic balance.

9
00:00:17.657 --> 00:00:19.768
Segregation: each parent passes on

10
00:00:19.768 --> 00:00:21.488
one allele for a trait.

11
00:00:21.488 --> 00:00:24.019
Independent assortment: different traits sort

12
00:00:24.019 --> 00:00:25.294
independently.

13
00:00:25.653 --> 00:00:27.714
Allele frequencies stay the same

14
00:00:27.714 --> 00:00:30.282
across generations unless mutation,

15
00:00:30.282 --> 00:00:32.524
selection, migration or drift change

16
00:00:32.524 --> 00:00:33.401
them.

17
00:00:34.075 --> 00:00:35.252
Your turn.

18
00:00:35.252 --> 00:00:37.455
Which one doesn't disturb it?
